{
  "capitulo": 5,
  "titulo_es": "Fui al mercado",
  "titulo": { "en": "I went to the market" },
  "intro": { "en": "Ser, ir, tener and hacer are irregular in the indefinido." },
  "palabras": {
    "fui": { "en": "I went, I was", "pron": "fwi", "cat": "verb", "nota": "Fui is both ir and ser in the past." },
    "fue": { "en": "he/she went, it was", "pron": "fwe", "cat": "verb" },
    "tuve": { "en": "I had", "pron": "TU-be", "cat": "verb" },
    "hice": { "en": "I did, I made", "pron": "I-the", "cat": "verb", "consejo": "In Spain the c sounds like th. In Latin America it sounds like s." },
    "hizo": { "en": "he/she did", "pron": "I-tho", "cat": "verb" },
    "al mercado": { "en": "to the market", "pron": "al mer-KA-do", "cat": "expression", "nota": "A + el becomes al." },
    "la compra": { "en": "the shopping", "pron": "la KOM-pra", "genero": "f" },
    "muy bueno": { "en": "very good", "pron": "mwi BWE-no", "cat": "expression" }
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Four irregular verbs",
      "texto": "These four do not use the regular endings.\n\n- ir and ser: **fui, fuiste, fue, fuimos, fuisteis, fueron**\n- tener: **tuve, tuviste, tuvo**\n- hacer: **hice, hiciste, hizo**\n\nContext tells ir from ser. **Fui al mercado** is went. **La película fue buena** is was."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "titulo": "Yo, yesterday",
      "columnas": ["Verb", "yo"],
      "filas": [
        ["ir / ser", "fui"],
        ["tener", "tuve"],
        ["hacer", "hice"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": "Saturday",
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Ayer fui al mercado.",
          "en": "Yesterday I went to the market.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Ayer", "yesterday"],
            ["fui", "I went"],
            ["al mercado", "to the market"]
          ]
        },
        {
